# Copy to `.env.local` only if you want to change recognition behaviour.
# Nothing here is required: the app defaults to free, local recognition.

# Which recognizer the add form uses.
#   heuristic (default) — free, local, offline; fills colors only
#   ai                  — calls the server function at /api/recognize
VITE_RECOGNITION_PROVIDER=heuristic

# --- Server-side only (used by server/recognize.ts) --------------------------
# Never prefix these with VITE_. A VITE_ variable is compiled into the public
# JavaScript bundle and is readable by anyone who visits the site.
#
# The optional cloud provider is NOT part of the zero-dollar default. Use it
# only with a key you own and a backend you control.
# RECOGNITION_API_KEY=
# RECOGNITION_API_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
# RECOGNITION_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
#
# Abuse protection for the reference function. The in-memory limiter is only a
# best-effort single-instance integration point; a public deployment also needs
# a platform/distributed rate limit, authentication or another abuse control,
# and a spending cap in the provider dashboard.
# RECOGNITION_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=20
# Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call a cross-origin function.
# CORS is not authentication; leave empty for a same-origin deployment.
# RECOGNITION_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://example.com
